cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dbmask in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dbmask: discover, mask, and validate sensitive data in SQL databases"
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python toolkit that discovers sensitive columns in SQL
  databases (pattern heuristics, manual overrides, optional LLM fallback),
  masks them with deterministic, referentially-consistent fake values, and
  validates afterwards that the masking actually happened — one auditable
  workflow for producing safe copies of production data.
